### Autowired Tools via MCP

All entities and actions/functions defined in the CAP service are automatically made available as MCP tools to the agent locally. The tools are constructed and served as documented in the MCP Adapter (/docs/guides/ai/cap-mcp) guide.

We can see the effects of that in the log output, for example, when asked to _"list books"_, the agent queried the service's `Books` entity via the `query` (/docs/guides/ai/cap-mcp#-query-entity) tool:

```sh [Log output for "List books"]
[agents] - CatalogService request {
  text: 'list books', ...
}
[mcp] - CatalogService describe {
  entities: [ 'Books' ]
}
[mcp] - CatalogService query {
  cql: 'SELECT ID, title, author, genre, ... from Books'
}
```

Similarly, when asked to _"order wuthering heights"_, the agent eventually invoked the appropriate service action via the `call` (/docs/guides/ai/cap-mcp#-call-action) tool:

```sh [Log output for "Order wuthering heights"]
[agents] - CatalogService request {
  text: 'order wuthering heights', ...
}
[mcp] - CatalogService - call submitOrder {
  book: 201, quantity: 1
}
```

